#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133660 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb06ab09-4bf5-5f87-a6cf-d71c2c9d3296" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "da211af4-8acc-56f9-9b5f-8f2d9b026c70" :question/math-academy-id "e-7395" :question/problem "A coin is biased so that the probability of it landing on heads is $0.4.$ The coin is tossed $7$ times. What is the mean number of times the coin lands on heads?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin lands on heads. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=7$ tosses\n\n- the probability of landing on heads for each toss is $p=0.4$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X\\sim B(7,0.4).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean of the number of times the coin lands on heads is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(7)(0.4) \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133661 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9e1f419-8442-5192-a1fa-44b5bedeff56" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "6f20b6aa-5867-5079-ac47-ba1f3f6486f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7396" :question/problem "An archer practices shooting $12$ arrows at a target. The archer has a $50\\%$ chance of hitting the bull's eye. What is the variance in the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ shots\n\n- the probability of hitting the bull's eye for each arrow is $p=50\\%=0.5$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X\\sim B(12,0.5).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\n So, the variance of the number of arrows hitting the bull's eye is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(12)(0.5)(1-0.5) \\\\  & =(6)(0.5) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133662 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c66a7ba5-1019-56bd-b915-bb725ee4a499" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Deviation of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "c33c8f5f-6640-5d53-8803-8b4cfaccea6a" :question/math-academy-id "e-7397" :question/problem "A fair five-sided die is rolled $8$ times. What is the standard deviation of the number of times we get an even number? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times we get an even number.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=8$ rolls of the die\n\n- the probability of getting an even number (i.e., a $2,$ or $4$) on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\dfrac{2}{5} .\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X\\sim B\\left(8,\\dfrac25\\right).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{SD}[X] = \\sqrt{\\textrm{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of times we get an even number is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot (1-\\frac{2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1.92} \\\\  & =1.386\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb06ab09-4bf5-5f87-a6cf-d71c2c9d3296" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25cf9ed6-5d80-5316-a85f-81ae68ce439d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421938} {:answer/id #uuid "33ea5317-6dc1-5052-854f-8321410625d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421941} {:answer/id #uuid "bd86f57c-83b3-5a48-8104-a8621c5314c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421964} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ab47f4-d3b2-5da5-8dc7-53a759699c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421968} {:answer/id #uuid "dde0bec6-b353-548b-907e-68f5d5bd0cf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd86f57c-83b3-5a48-8104-a8621c5314c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421964} :answer-field/id #uuid "f16f7ac3-5d3e-5fdc-9751-952a50dea70c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f3bf9f8-8f58-5a26-b354-f87af2b2eaa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130752" :question/problem "A tennis player has a $60%$ chance of winning each match in a $5$-match tournament. What is the mean number of matches that the player wins?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of matches that the player wins.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=5$ matches\n\n- the probability of winning each match is $p=60%=0.6$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,0.6).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of matches that the player wins is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(5)(0.60) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb06ab09-4bf5-5f87-a6cf-d71c2c9d3296" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4bdfc2-c0e9-5af4-abe8-067d3285da99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421932} {:answer/id #uuid "162e61c6-2672-53bc-b506-42b887c80bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421935} {:answer/id #uuid "6856acca-0b10-524b-b6c0-3ba8ffe6d469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421951} {:answer/id #uuid "c11f043f-d0d7-5366-8f1e-26ca782b6852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421965} {:answer/id #uuid "d743d3d8-0ac8-570a-9105-9ddcd4674ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6856acca-0b10-524b-b6c0-3ba8ffe6d469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421951} :answer-field/id #uuid "683d39b0-2df2-5987-be72-7499346048ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25a0a850-41a7-52c6-b901-d7ad5795dcd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130755" :question/problem "A fair coin is tossed $20$ times. What is the mean number of tails that occur?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of tails that occur. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=20$ tosses\n\n- since the coin is fair, the probability of landing on tails for each toss is $p=\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(20,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of tails that occur is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(20)(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9e1f419-8442-5192-a1fa-44b5bedeff56" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a1da0bd-fbca-576c-9d98-2c5457624d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421931} {:answer/id #uuid "34b2a832-8cee-5042-b5f3-310a15c0aa97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421942} {:answer/id #uuid "3f592e8f-e602-59d7-9c67-f601dddbe2e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421944} {:answer/id #uuid "85974766-468e-56eb-ba05-3ae52a9770fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421956} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc18f76-a69e-5f09-9bb8-5aa58c800ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fc18f76-a69e-5f09-9bb8-5aa58c800ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421960} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb92a3f-b47d-5759-a6af-54bb075b7bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35949c7a-955a-5bb4-ba6f-41e4641f0ce2" :question/math-academy-id "q-130763" :question/problem "There are $15$ gift boxes in a lucky gift machine, $6$ of which have a toy inside. After being picked, the gift box will be replaced by another one of the same value. Six kids are waiting in line for their turn to use it. What is the variance of the number of kids who get a toy?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of kids who get a toy from the $6$ kids.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=6$ kids that are waiting in line for their turn to use the machine\n\n- since there are $6$ toys out of a total of $15$ gift boxes, then the probability that a kid gets a toy is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{6}{15}=\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(6,\\frac{2}{5}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of kids who get a toy is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot (1-\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9e1f419-8442-5192-a1fa-44b5bedeff56" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e19085-b196-5d51-9863-47908156eca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{125}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421937} {:answer/id #uuid "5d31d5ff-3374-591a-a832-e6af48967464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{75}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421949} {:answer/id #uuid "7a68e62a-0aac-5912-9c1d-b67fbcb42582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421952} {:answer/id #uuid "84bd8c58-0d9c-5855-a5e9-f875f7625f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{72}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421955} {:answer/id #uuid "887d0da7-9a5f-5923-9b6d-66308de467fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{75}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "887d0da7-9a5f-5923-9b6d-66308de467fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{75}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421958} :answer-field/id #uuid "e996cded-d3ba-5d9b-afa2-4b9d6ae9a669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f3fbaf6-b15b-53c6-9279-fcc77fd83e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130764" :question/problem "A  fair octahedral die with sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $8$ is rolled $25$ times. What is the variance of the number of times we get a number divisible by $3?$" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of times we get a number divisible by $3.$\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=25$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a number divisible by $3$ (i.e., a $3$ or a $6$) on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(25,\\frac{1}{4}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of times we get a number divisible by $3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{75}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c66a7ba5-1019-56bd-b915-bb725ee4a499" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Deviation of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb983d5-2b7b-5838-bc2a-1666de24661f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.394" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421936} {:answer/id #uuid "56c30780-7d07-5a2e-8519-69c2c3b635fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.154" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421947} {:answer/id #uuid "8b38c6aa-a639-5c59-a6f3-477d51479873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.375" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421959} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f2f5eb-23ba-5d31-9a39-bfc963eeafaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.518" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421966} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f09300-30a4-50ed-beaa-6f1198f91050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.362" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bb983d5-2b7b-5838-bc2a-1666de24661f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.394" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421936} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbcc53b2-5f84-54cb-ad5c-a16cf94b1669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3dde14a-c77b-5290-8e8d-52f3133ef7aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130766" :question/problem "A new drug has a $64%$ probability of curing a patient within a week. If $50$ patients are treated, what is the standard deviation of the number of cured patients within a week? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of cured patients within a week.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=50$ patients in the sample\n\n- the probability that the new drug has cured a patient within a week is $p=64%=0.64$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(50,0.64).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of cured patients within a week is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(50)(0.64)(1-0.64)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(50)(0.64)(0.36)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11.52} \\\\  & ≈3.394\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c66a7ba5-1019-56bd-b915-bb725ee4a499" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Deviation of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "155de04a-19c5-548a-9a38-8b17697942c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421934} {:answer/id #uuid "396fb0b5-0937-562e-b292-d871531d1399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.918" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421943} {:answer/id #uuid "6519a704-3057-55cd-bed2-1c31319df05d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.268" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421950} {:answer/id #uuid "88059b2a-96be-58d2-99c2-cf71c816f2f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.897" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421957} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1c6f72-1a3a-554f-a780-a0e87d75a879" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.459" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "396fb0b5-0937-562e-b292-d871531d1399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.918" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421943} :answer-field/id #uuid "33864cf7-e227-514a-994b-4fc9fe7a2ef7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd4098b0-44f3-5628-89ab-3a85dd72d97e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130883" :question/problem "An infectious flu virus is spreading through a school. The probability of a randomly selected student having the flu next week is $0.2.$ If a class has $23$ students, what is the standard deviation of the number of students having the flu next week? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of students having the flu next week.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=23$ students in the class\n\n- the probability of selecting a student having the flu next week is $0.2$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(23,0.2).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of students having the flu next week is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(23)(0.2)(1-0.2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(23)(0.2)(0.8)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3.68} \\\\  & ≈1.918\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb06ab09-4bf5-5f87-a6cf-d71c2c9d3296" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc743751-a4dc-560b-9dd4-b09dfa719464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133171} {:answer/id #uuid "f8694805-7839-5d4e-ae3f-39a8e8e377f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133172} {:answer/id #uuid "6443dd9d-d5f7-5747-8bef-c800ccff1405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133173} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd6c915-c1a5-59a4-989c-437e44acd2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133174} {:answer/id #uuid "782e821e-f89c-50e4-b77c-1aaef0d0f9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "782e821e-f89c-50e4-b77c-1aaef0d0f9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133175} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a45b79-0c0c-51c7-9561-ba465de3caeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b1810d9-74ee-5cc5-b570-fc2f66f9da2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-84488" :question/problem "A softball team has a $60%$ chance of winning each game in a $12$-game season. What is the mean number of games that the team wins during a season?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of games that the team wins in a given season. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ games\n\n- the probability of winning each game is $p=60%=0.6$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(12,0.6).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean of the number of games won is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(12)(0.6) \\\\  & =7.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb06ab09-4bf5-5f87-a6cf-d71c2c9d3296" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b56ca0da-9985-599d-80a8-cee5c4008aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133177} {:answer/id #uuid "ec02075b-29b7-5bc5-a31b-79aa961e36f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133178} {:answer/id #uuid "fd6dcd85-9524-5337-8c98-12b0ee153e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133179} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc27491-1910-51c1-a130-9bc8c1a71513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133180} {:answer/id #uuid "5f88a268-a60c-5086-bbad-72a92a6f39f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b56ca0da-9985-599d-80a8-cee5c4008aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133177} :answer-field/id #uuid "27eb67c2-f7bd-508b-99c4-0eec717abe9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41a88797-8a0f-5a6f-a8b9-7def35d693e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-84490" :question/problem "A fair six-sided die is rolled $7$ times. What is the mean of the number of times that the outcome of a single roll is a $2$ or a $3?$" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times a $2$ or $3$ is rolled.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=7$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a $2$ or $3$ on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(7,\\frac{1}{3}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of times we get a $2$ or a $3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9e1f419-8442-5192-a1fa-44b5bedeff56" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a67e27e-44af-5360-8715-296d8aa8f8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133183} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ed4a85-f7b1-57f4-ad92-83fb9147d902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133184} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8fded3-c72f-5c90-9464-ecad8a0470fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133185} {:answer/id #uuid "15d61f03-c16d-58bc-a1a1-29d768ab7f9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133186} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5da85f-e7d2-5690-8235-e4df538b2d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e5da85f-e7d2-5690-8235-e4df538b2d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133187} :answer-field/id #uuid "e88a4196-cc79-5e10-bfb8-147ace0b9d95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b33ecee-6694-5f5b-b468-fb60f3c15a41" :question/math-academy-id "q-84492" :question/problem "A football team has a $30%$ chance of winning each game in a $20$-game season. What is the variance of the number of games that the football team wins during a season?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of games that the team wins in a given season. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=20$ games\n\n- the probability of winning each game is $p=30%=0.3$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(20,0.3).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of games won is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(20)(0.3)(1-0.3) \\\\  & =(6)(0.7) \\\\  & =4.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9e1f419-8442-5192-a1fa-44b5bedeff56" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e44cce-8bca-5ac8-80a0-02abd7b3acd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421933} {:answer/id #uuid "4fa3b4a5-cc48-533b-bd88-30d43ccbc53c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421946} {:answer/id #uuid "5c47db2b-5f15-55e5-9a8b-2c3d636f340a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421948} {:answer/id #uuid "7a869429-9bb2-5c02-8d64-f99c5767b4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421953} {:answer/id #uuid "dbd63a4b-3acc-57cf-a187-bd16d36c3981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c47db2b-5f15-55e5-9a8b-2c3d636f340a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421948} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dd00208-7396-5c4f-b789-94854564cf74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed91a13d-0a09-59c4-bf60-d5ad7aad9e5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-84691" :question/problem "An archer practices shooting $16$ arrows at a target. The archer has a $25%$ chance of hitting the bull's eye. What is the variance in the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=16$ shots\n\n- the probability of hitting the bull's eye for each arrow is $p=25%=0.25$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(16,0.25).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\n So, the variance of the number of arrows hitting the bull's eye is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(16)(0.25)(1-0.25) \\\\  & =(4)(0.75) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb06ab09-4bf5-5f87-a6cf-d71c2c9d3296" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fec556e-e148-5b1e-97a7-c14be487a96c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421940} {:answer/id #uuid "4124268c-a67c-5426-94fd-b3b803fb7198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421945} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd5208b-1965-5729-baf4-fee9daa9dd7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421954} {:answer/id #uuid "a438da50-52c7-56e2-9c8d-f943b1b94b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421961} {:answer/id #uuid "af0cc9f5-7af8-51a0-9383-5f1def95ba05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a438da50-52c7-56e2-9c8d-f943b1b94b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421961} :answer-field/id #uuid "f267f788-271e-50ed-b945-f7aa83b94fe5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a15eeec-0407-53e4-9770-0d33f30c6d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-84745" :question/problem "A fair eight-sided die is rolled $6$ times. What is the mean number of times that the outcome of a single roll is either $2,5,$ or $7?$" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times a $2$ or $5$ or $7$ is rolled.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=6$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a $2,5,$ or $7$ on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(6,\\frac{3}{8}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of times we get a $2$ or a $5$ or a $7$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9e1f419-8442-5192-a1fa-44b5bedeff56" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance of a Binomial Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c51642-996d-5135-870c-db34a80b53f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421929} {:answer/id #uuid "07cebf32-de57-5ac9-b739-e5dd0c9c0388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421930} {:answer/id #uuid "2ba091fe-7823-5e7d-9d7b-281b39b773d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421939} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d52625-39ab-5725-8e70-b6d00bcc3df8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421962} {:answer/id #uuid "e3dfbebf-b841-570e-af01-fbb924f4028f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ba091fe-7823-5e7d-9d7b-281b39b773d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421939} :answer-field/id #uuid "52456990-d9af-5708-ac87-59cf743cda06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afe30003-2595-50a2-8b60-8382c78a5f23" :question/math-academy-id "q-89408" :question/problem "A student answers a multiple-choice test choosing each answer at random. If the test has $20$ questions, and each question has $4$ possible answers with only one correct answer, what is the variance of the number of correct answers?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of correct answers.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=20$ questions\n\n- the probability of selecting the correct answer in each question is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(20,\\frac{1}{4}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of correct answers is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
